      "section": "🔒 Security model",
      "text": "- All routes (`/api/photo-skins/*`) sit behind a same-origin fence\n  (Sec-Fetch-Site / Origin): cross-site webpages cannot read, import or\n  delete your photos.\n- Uploads are validated by file magic bytes, not by name or declared\n  content-type — a renamed SVG or executable is rejected (415). SVG is\n  deliberately unsupported (script risk).\n- Uploads are capped at 25MB (413) and written atomically (tmp + rename).\n- Stored ids are generated and validated against a whitelist regex, so no\n  path can escape the store directory.\n- Web-Reach search providers and tools run in the host process (there is no\n  browser-exposed route), and every outbound fetch is SSRF-gated: only public\n  http(s) URLs are fetched, and loopback / link-local / private / reserved IP\n  ranges, plus cloud-metadata hostnames and IP-obfuscation forms, are refused.\n  Redirects are re-validated and capped; responses are timeout-bounded (15-20s)\n  and size-capped (2 MiB); provider/tool execution honours the turn's\n  cancellation signal. The Exa hosted-MCP endpoint\n  (https://mcp.exa.ai/mcp) passes the same SSRF gate.\n- The DuckDuckGo search path sends only a text query term (never a URL) and\n  reports the decoded result"
